          "display_name": "DeepSeek",
          "execution_status": "SUCCESS",
          "provider": "deepseek",
          "rank": 1,
          "reason": "Q3 revenue rose 26% to $85.4M, EPS was $0.27 versus $0.06, and management raised FY26 revenue and EBITDA guidance. Shares closed up 14% at a 52-week high on heavy volume with after-hours follow-through, supporting near-term post-earnings drift and estimate revisions.",
          "risk": "NexoBrid included roughly $3M of one-time BARDA revenue, and the stock is overbought after a 14% gap; losing $50 support could trigger a fast gap-fill.",
